WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000 align:center
♪ at dusk, in Decayed Sector - Outer Rim, Cautious hope amidst overwhelming decay.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.300 align:center
The Hero: Another echo. Faint. Barely a whisper against the void.

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.600 align:center
The Hero: The Archive. A myth, they said. Just… dust.

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.900 align:center
The Hero: But even dust remembers. Doesn’t it?

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:24.200 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Sundered Archive - Outer Chambers, Growing apprehension and the weight of forgotten truths.

6
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.500 align:center
The Hero: No… this isn't decay. This is… erasure.

7
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.800 align:center
The Hero: Billions of years. Entire civilizations. Gone. Not forgotten, but… un-made.

8
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.100 align:center
The Hero: And a guardian. Protecting… what? The nothingness?

9
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:42.400 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Sundered Archive - Data Antechamber, Urgent dread and hardened resolve.

10
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.700 align:center
The Hero: This isn't just about saving memories. It's about saving… everything.

11
00:00:46.1000 --> 00:00:49.1000 align:center
The Hero: That guardian. It stands between us and… truth.

12
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.300 align:center
The Hero: I won't let another truth fade.

13
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.600 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Sundered Archive - Collapsing Corridors, Desperate struggle against overwhelming odds.

14
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.900 align:center
The Hero: Void energy… it's actively tearing it apart.

15
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.200 align:center
The Hero: Faster. It's moving faster.

16
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.500 align:center
The Hero: This isn't just a force. It's… hungry.

17
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:16.800 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Sundered Archive - Central Absorption Chamber, Crushing sense of futility and sacrifice.

18
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.100 align:center
The Hero: It’s not just destroying structures… it's consuming the data itself.

19
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.400 align:center
The Hero: Every shard of knowledge… gone. Forever.

20
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.700 align:center
The Hero: This isn't just a fight. It's an elegy.

21
00:01:27.1000 --> 00:01:33.1000 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Sundered Archive - Central Absorption Chamber, Desperate, escalating struggle.

22
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.300 align:center
The Hero: No! Not that data!

23
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.600 align:center
The Hero: It's too strong. Too… pervasive.

24
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.900 align:center
The Hero: Then I won't fight it directly. I'll… starve it.

25
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:50.200 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Sundered Archive - Data-Core Nexus, Catastrophic urgency and impending doom.

26
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.500 align:center
The Hero: Now! Disrupt the field!

27
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.800 align:center
The Hero: It's… collapsing! The whole sector!

28
00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.100 align:center
The Hero: No escape. Not now.

29
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:06.400 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Sundered Archive - Collapsing Data-Core Nexus, Futility, sacrifice, and a desperate grasp for survival.

30
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.700 align:center
The Hero: The core! I have to… secure it!

31
00:02:09.1000 --> 00:02:11.1000 align:center
The Hero: My arm… it's fusing…

32
00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.300 align:center
The Hero: Worth it. For the memory.

33
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:21.600 align:center
♪ at dawn, in Void Edge - Archive Remains, A costly, Pyrrhic 'victory' and exhaustion.

34
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.900 align:center
The Hero: Out… I'm out.

35
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.200 align:center
The Hero: The Archive… gone. All of it.

36
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.500 align:center
The Hero: But I have this. This sliver.

37
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.800 align:center
♪ at dawn, in Desolate Vantage Point - Cosmic Debris Field, Terrified realization and dawning horror.

38
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.100 align:center
The Hero: No. This can't be right.

39
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.400 align:center
The Hero: The entropy… it's not natural. It's… guided.

40
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.700 align:center
The Hero: Someone is doing this. Someone… or something.

41
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:53.000 align:center
♪ at dawn, in Desolate Vantage Point - Cosmic Debris Field, Hardened, terrified resolve in the face of a greater, personal threat.

42
00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.300 align:center
The Hero: A shepherd of oblivion. And I've just announced my presence.

43
00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.600 align:center
The Hero: They know I'm here. They know I have this.

44
00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:05.900 align:center
The Hero: Let them come. I won't let another memory die.
